      "prompt": "Write $\\dfrac{{{p}}}{{{v}{a:+}}} - \\dfrac{{{q}}}{{{v}{b:+}}}$ over $({v}{a:+})({v}{b:+})$. Type the top, simplified.",
      "widget": {
        "kind": "expression",
        "answer": "{poly(v; m, c0)}",
        "form": "simplified"
      },
      "wrong": [
        {
          "id": "sign-lost",
          "tex": "{poly(v; m, lost)}",
          "line": "The minus applies to the whole of ${q:c}({v}{a:+})$, so its last term changes sign too."
        },
        {
          "id": "own-bottoms",
          "tex": "{poly(v; m, own)}",
          "line": "You multiplied each top by its own bottom. ${p}$ is multiplied by $({v}{b:+})$, the bracket it lacks.",
          "when": "p*a - q*b != p*b + q*a"
        }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Over $({v}{a:+})({v}{b:+})$ the top is ${p}({v}{b:+}) - {q:c}({v}{a:+})$, with the second top in a bracket.",
        "That is ${poly(v; p, p*b)} {poly(v; -q, -q*a)} = {poly(v; m, c0)}$."
      ]
    },
