      "let": {
        "ll": "k - aa - bb",
        "cc": "-aa*k",
        "nr": "-r",
        "ns": "-s"
      },
      "prompt": "Solve $\\dfrac{{{aa}}}{{x}} + \\dfrac{{{bb}}}{{x + {k}}} = 1$. Give both values of $x$.",
      "widget": {
        "kind": "numeric",
        "answers": [
          "{r}",
          "{s}"
        ],
        "unordered": true,
        "tol": {
          "abs": 0
        }
      },
      "wrong": [
        {
          "id": "signs",
          "value": "{nr}, {ns}",
          "line": "Those are the roots with their signs changed. A factor $(x{nr:+})$ gives $x = {r}$."
        }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Multiply every term by $x(x + {k})$: ${aa:c}(x + {k}) + {bb}x = x(x + {k})$.",
        "So ${poly(x; 1, ll, cc)} = (x{nr:+})(x{ns:+}) = 0$.",
        "Neither root makes a bottom zero, so $x = {r}$ or $x = {s}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "reject-root",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "reject a root that makes a bottom zero",
      "vars": {
